menu "SynthDef memory placement"
    config SYNTHDEF_INTERNAL_VOICE_ARENA_SAMPLES
        int "Internal-memory arena for smaller stateful voices (float samples)"
        depends on SYNTHDEF_FM1_COMPAT
        range 0 16896
        default 0
        help
            Optionally reserves up to 66 KiB for voices whose state fits, including
            each non-compact Rings model. Larger voices keep the full 1 MiB
            PSRAM arena. No delay capacity or sample precision is reduced.
            Disabled by default; the measured gain is small relative to RAM cost.
    config SYNTHDEF_INTERNAL_RINGS
        bool "Keep Rings processing routines in internal instruction RAM"
        default y if SYNTHDEF_FM1_COMPAT
        default n
        help
            Places existing Rings code in internal instruction RAM without
            changing algorithms, table values, precision or string capacity.
    config SYNTHDEF_INTERNAL_ADAPTER
        bool "Keep audio control and PCM routines in internal instruction RAM"
        default y
        help
            Avoids flash instruction misses in the small per-block adapter.
            The sound algorithms and PCM rounding remain unchanged.
    config SYNTHDEF_INTERNAL_KERNELS
        bool "Keep admitted-voice rendering kernels in internal instruction RAM"
        default y
        help
            Avoids contention with display code for the flash instruction cache.
            Only linker placement changes; engine source and math stay pinned.
    config SYNTHDEF_INTERNAL_SINE
        bool "Keep the immutable sine lookup table in internal RAM"
        default n
        help
            Uses 32772 bytes of internal RAM to avoid flash data-cache misses
            in the admitted oscillator. No engine code or table bytes change.
endmenu
